 ScenarioA;oks;really;boardsays;ok;result
⍝ ── A — Double-book (at rest) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
⍝ Four clerks go for the same free seat at once. Only one should win, and the count
⍝ should still match the seats taken. You can see this fault at rest: once the run
⍝ ends, several clerks report success for one seat, or the count no longer matches the
⍝ seats actually taken.
 NewSeats 10
 oks←⎕TSYNC Book&¨4⍴5               ⍝ four clerks, one seat (#5)
 really←+/SEATS                     ⍝ seats actually taken (the single source of truth)
 boardsays←(≢SEATS)-Remaining 0     ⍝ what the board thinks is taken
 ok←(1=+/oks)∧(boardsays=really)∧(1=really)
 result←'FAIL' 'PASS'⊃⍨⎕IO+ok
 ⎕←'A double-book : successes=',(⍕+/oks),' board=',(⍕boardsays),' really=',⍕really
 ⎕←'Scenario A: ',result
